{"skill":{"slug":"academic-research-hub","displayName":"Academic Research Hub"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1770539628030,"changelog":"Initial release of Academic Research Hub – a multi-source academic literature search and management toolkit.\n\n- Search academic papers across arXiv, PubMed, and Semantic Scholar from a single command-line interface.\n- Download PDFs, extract citations, and generate bibliographies in multiple formats (BibTeX, RIS, JSON, Markdown).\n- Retrieve comprehensive metadata: title, authors, abstract, publication details, citation counts, and references.\n- Flexible filtering by source, category, publication type, date range, and citation count.\n- Save, format, and manage research results via CLI options for academic workflows.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":19164,"sha256":"10213493b3d39c28239b766fa91b84643f0f5532e795c39c6ef361d3984811fd","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/readme.md","size":6912,"sha256":"9183907f60e3cbf1a45b8b5db8a931a697b30608f6ea39476af211bc48b8a457","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/requirements.txt","size":276,"sha256":"2659583c5256479a7735b17e05279698e5ee5970408664798766ae0da9e97e37","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/research.py","size":24529,"sha256":"9c8b39b7eddf6152aa577ed0db7ced8d1ec9a5aca7f738a577a31899dfc184cb","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2434,"sha256":"a07020cf1612f1f04c9950a43981a5e4ad44ddb1e5db12108baef2022b47bd86","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789039375989,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"16ee241003472fe79b1301d0a326ebb94773e10d52bacffdd94326dc10510b05","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/16ee241003472fe79b1301d0a326ebb94773e10d52bacffdd94326dc10510b05","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: academic-research-hub\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill bundle is classified as benign. All code and documentation align with the stated purpose of searching, downloading, and managing academic papers. The `scripts/research.py` uses legitimate Python libraries (arxiv, semanticscholar, biopython, requests) to interact with academic databases and download PDFs, writing files to user-specified or default directories. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts in `SKILL.md` or `references/readme.md` to mislead the agent into harmful actions. The installation instructions even include a warning against `--break-system-packages`, promoting secure practices.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162178249},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":58,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":15,"checkedAt":1789039375989},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed academic-search tool with expected network access and optional local file downloads, but users should treat its dependency and download handling as ordinary security hardening gaps.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Outbound API calls and user-directed output files are proportionate for the stated purpose; PDF downloads lack size, content-type, redirect, and hostname validation, so users should keep download scope modest.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation guidance uses pip packages with open-ended versions and includes some packages not used by the implementation, which increases supply-chain exposure but does not show malicious installation behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The activation language is broad and the docs mention unsupported options such as Google Scholar, citations, full-text links, and include-references, but the implemented script is limited to explicit CLI searches and arXiv PDF downloads.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, privilege escalation, background services, credential harvesting, memory modification, or automatic execution hooks were found in the inspected artifacts.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifacts consistently present an academic research helper for searching arXiv, PubMed, and Semantic Scholar, formatting citations, saving results, and optionally downloading papers.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this only in a virtual environment, avoid elevated privileges, and prefer pinned dependencies or a reviewed lockfile. Use downloads deliberately, keep result counts small, and choose output directories you are comfortable modifying. Be aware that the docs overstate some features and mention Google Scholar-related dependencies even though the inspected script does not implement Google Scholar support.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Network access and local output are expected for this research tool; lack of an explicit permission section is a documentation/scoping gap rather than evidence of hidden behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: The trigger is broad for scholarly research tasks, but sensitive actions such as downloads and file output are exposed as explicit command options.\n[E1] expected: External academic service URLs are expected data sources for the skill; no artifact-backed secret collection or unrelated transmission was found.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: Documentation is inconsistent about Google Scholar and the scholarly dependency, while the script does not implement Google Scholar access; this is misleading capability documentation, not active concealed scraping.\n[SQP-2] expected: PDF download and output-file creation are core advertised features, though clearer warnings about local writes and batch storage use would be appropriate.\n[SC1] expected: The unpinned dependencies are a real supply-chain hardening issue, but the packages align with academic search and HTTP functionality.\n[SC4] expected: Potential vulnerable dependency versions cannot be ruled out because versions are not pinned; this supports user caution, not a malicious verdict.\n[T08] expected: The static supply-chain finding is supported by requirements.txt and installation docs, but it does not demonstrate a currently malicious package or purpose-incompatible behavior.\n[T09] expected: The PDF downloader does trust externally supplied URLs and writes full responses to disk, which is a real validation weakness in a purpose-aligned, user-invoked download feature.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789039375989}}}}}